# Lesson 5, your Exercise 1, completed with East-West cards.
title: Your Exercise 1: partner shows spades
id: L05-01
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.5
student: S
board: 1
dealer: N
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AJ75   Q8     KJ62   AQ2
  E  T6     5432   Q93    9864
  S  KQ84   KJT7   T5     KT7
  W  932    A96    A874   J53

auction:
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 2C     = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
  W Pass
  N 2S     = Four spades, not four hearts
  E Pass
  S 4S*    = Four spades and game values
     key: You have found an 8-card spade fit, and 12 points opposite 15-17 is enough for game.
     not 3S: 3♠ only invites. With 12 points you know there is enough for game.
     not 3NT: You have found an 8-card spade fit. Play in spades.
     not 2NT: 2NT invites. You have enough for game, and a spade fit.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Your 2♣ asked about majors, and North's 2♠ found the 4-4 spade fit. With 12
  points opposite 15-17, your side has 27-29: plenty for game. 4♠ is the
  obvious bid. North is declarer, because North bid spades first, and so East
  will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E C9  S C7  W CJ  N CQ
  2   N SA  E S6  S S4  W S2
      note: Declarer starts drawing trumps.
  3   N S5  E ST  S SK  W S3
      note: Keep drawing trumps.
  4   S SQ  W S9  N S7  E H2
      note: The opponents' trumps are all gone.
  5   S H7  W H6  N HQ  E H3
      note: Now set up dummy's hearts, starting with a low heart toward North's queen.
  6   N H8  E H4  S HJ  W HA
      note: West takes the ace. Dummy's ♥K and ♥T are now winners.
  7   W C5  N C2  E C8  S CK
  8   S HK  W H9  N D2  E H5
      note: Declarer throws a diamond from hand on the good heart.
  9   S HT  W D4  N D6  E C6
      note: And another.
  10  S DT  W D7  N DK  E D3
      note: Lead toward the ♦K: if West has the ace, the king wins.
  11  N CA  E C4  S CT  W C3
      note: Cash the club winner.
  12  N DJ  E D9  S D5  W DA
      note: Give up the last diamond trick.
  13  W D8  N SJ  E DQ  S S8
      note: 11 tricks: 4♠ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: draw trumps, then knock out the ♥A so the rest of the
  hearts become winners.

  4♠ made 11 tricks. 3NT would also have made here, with ten tricks, so this
  time the wrong bid would not have cost the game. But 4♠ scored more, and the
  trump suit gave declarer control. With an 8-card major fit, the suit
  contract is usually the better bet.
